{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/340319-the-lost-legion-trapped-in-the-abyss","id":340319,"title":"The Lost Legion trapped in the Abyss","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-14T18:38:50-08:00","id":340319,"title":"The Lost Legion trapped in the Abyss","content":"In Umbra Revised there was a few short paragraphs about the Lost Legion being trapped in the Abyss and taking up camp on the Iron Road. These unfortunate wraiths were trapped in the realm and unable to return to the Underworld. I'm taking this for inspiration for a chronicle idea for my current group of players. How would the unique metaphysics of being a Wraith be affected by being trapped in the Abyss? Would they be so far removed from the Hivemind that thorns might be affected? Would they be able to regain Pathos if they follow their passions while in this place? What happens if they lose all their Corpus? Would a harrowing follow or would it just be the end? How might they escape from this place? I've got a lot of potential rattling around in my head over this, I just want to make sure I've got a good grasp of the metaphysical basics before I start really fleshing this idea out.<br /> <br /> Any takers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:17:35-07:00","id":445901,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that the Abyss is allegedly the home of the Fallen. Might be very interesting, indeed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:03:34-07:00","id":446192,"title":"","content":"it's heavily implied that oblivion, the abyss of the fallen and the abyss of the lasombra (and maybe werewolves but im not sure)<br /> are the exact same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T18:06:19-07:00","id":493067,"title":"","content":"The Abyss of the Fallen is adjacent to, or in, the Labyrinth. It's not Oblivion. However, the Abyss of the Fallen could be the same as the Abyss of the Lasombra. Likewise, although there may be a spiritual pathway between the Labyrinth in the Underworld and the Black Spiral labyrinth, the Wyrm appears to be active, while Oblivion is passive. One possible answer is that they're different sides of the same coin (the Yin and Yang sides of destruction). However, DtF also states the universe works on multiple levels, each of which is understood and perceived differently. Through a Mage lens (taking into account what we know of the KotE milieu), it's entirely possible that not only does it work on multiple levels, but it's also carved up into fragmented paradigms which fit together like a jigsaw of alternate but overlapping mythologies. As such, none of these things might ever fit together properly, although they might once have done far back in history (say, the First Age).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T19:19:02-07:00","id":527243,"title":"","content":"Well the Malfeans (described as looking like demons) are the ones who apparently carved the Labyrinth up from Oblivion, given the history at the beginning of 1st edition. We also learn that the Demons created the Underworld originally to save and safekeep mortal souls that died as the war of creation raged. The Isles hidden through the Sunless Sea from the byways was made by Charon (the Slayer rather than Emperor Charon the Wraith?) to keep the Angels from finding the mortal souls, like they did when they stormed the first attempt at hiding them, <i>Kasdeja</i>. It's also said that Charon dug deeper down, which formed the Labyrinth.<br /> Interestingly enough the Les Invisibles also refer to the Tempest as the Abyss... I do think that the way it's described that the Werewolf Abyss is most likely the Labyrinth and Oblivion of Wraith, they just seem so similar.<br /> I'm more interested in knowing just what Grandmother is though. Thats the one thing that interests me the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T05:34:25-07:00","id":527571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Old Rusty Pipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/340319-the-lost-legion-trapped-in-the-abyss#post340319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Umbra Revised there was a few short paragraphs about the Lost Legion being trapped in the Abyss and taking up camp on the Iron Road. These unfortunate wraiths were trapped in the realm and unable to return to the Underworld. I'm taking this for inspiration for a chronicle idea for my current group of players. How would the unique metaphysics of being a Wraith be affected by being trapped in the Abyss? Would they be so far removed from the Hivemind that thorns might be affected? Would they be able to regain Pathos if they follow their passions while in this place? What happens if they lose all their Corpus? Would a harrowing follow or would it just be the end? How might they escape from this place? I've got a lot of potential rattling around in my head over this, I just want to make sure I've got a good grasp of the metaphysical basics before I start really fleshing this idea out.<br /> <br /> Any takers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... for one, maybe their Shadow can slowly begin to manifestate Charms of the spirits (wyrm Charms) maybe even replacing them...<br /> then, after some time, the Wraiths would &quot;change&quot; developing Gnosis (as a meaning of survival) or Rage (as a byproduct of the Shadow and the Abyss) and thus becoming partially Spirits.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","